  "summary": "The Kohathites carry the holy things on their shoulders. The same word names the two pieces of the ephod where the memorial stones rest, and the supports under a bronze basin. Boundary descriptions follow the shoulder of a hill or settlement. Giving a stubborn shoulder is a gesture of refusal.",
