  "note": "Mehri and Jibbali retain the three consonants. Tigre and Geʿez have remodeled forms with an initial m. Turoyo katpo corresponds to Mlahsô kespo, while Barsky, Kalinin and Loesov trace the more frequent Turoyo katfo to Arabic. The Akkadian word names part of the breast of an animal. Its precise anatomical reference and its relationship to כָּתֵף are uncertain."
